	'fees_h2' => 'Intakes, registration and payment',
	'fees_b2_1' => 'Four intakes run in 2026: 12 January, 13 April, 7 September and 9 November. The registration fee of €45 is paid once, on enrolment, and it is separate from the course fee. It confirms your place on the intake after the written level and track proposal. Course fees may be paid in two instalments. The free 45-minute placement interview comes before any fee.',
	'fees_b2_2' => 'At week 5 of the term your level is reviewed. The school is open Monday to Thursday from 09:00 to 21:00, Friday from 09:00 to 17:00, and Saturday from 10:00 to 14:00 for placement interviews only. Sunday is closed. A placement evening is held on the first Thursday of each month at 18:30. Write to hello@kotobalanguage.example or call +31 10 555 0142.',
	'stories_intro' => 'Three learners describe how a course at the school was actually used: a Dutch evening course across three terms, two terms of English for a logistics team, and a settlement club for a newly arrived couple.',
	'stories_s1_h' => 'A customer-support team lead, from Beirut',
	'stories_s1_b_1' => 'A customer-support team lead moved from Beirut and joined the Dutch evening course at Kotoba Language. The evening course runs for 10 weeks, with two sessions of 90 minutes a week, and costs €590. The class is held to a maximum of 8. After three terms on that course, this learner sat the Dutch B1 exam. The path there began, as every path does, with a free 45-minute placement interview and a written level.',
	'stories_s1_b_2' => 'Registration was the one-time fee of €45. At week 5 of each term the level was reviewed. Dutch is one of six languages taught at the school, which was founded in 2016 and still teaches from Scheepmakerspassage 14, 3011 VH Rotterdam, Netherlands. The story we tell is the sitting itself, after three terms of evening classes.',
	'stories_s2_h' => 'A five-person logistics team',
	'stories_s2_b_1' => 'A five-person logistics team at a shipping agency took the workplace group track: two 10-week terms of English for work. A workplace group is taught on site for up to 6 people, so a team of five sits inside that limit. The fee for one 10-week term is €1,980. English for work is taught by Chidi Nwosu. Across the two terms the group stayed with the language of their own shifts, handovers and planning.',
	'stories_s2_b_2' => 'A private lesson, if one person had needed it, would have been €62 for 60 minutes. Placement before the first term was the free 45-minute interview, followed by a written level and the registration fee of €45. Week 5 of each term included a level review. The school teaches that English alongside Dutch, French, German, Mandarin and Japanese.',
	'stories_s3_h' => 'A newly arrived couple and their appointments',
	'stories_s3_b_1' => 'A newly arrived couple joined the settlement conversation club. The club runs for one term, weekly for 90 minutes, and costs €150. They now handle their own appointments in Dutch. That is the work of the settlement path: appointments, housing and schools, in a group no larger than 8. Ana Sol Vidal teaches Dutch for new arrivals, and Mariam Haddad teaches French on the same settlement track.',
	'stories_s3_b_2' => 'The couple\'s route into the club was the usual one. A free 45-minute placement interview, in person or online, produced a written level. Registration of €45 was paid once. The evening course, at €590 for 10 weeks, remains the fuller alternative when someone wants two sessions a week. Intakes in 2026 are 12 January, 13 April, 7 September and 9 November.',
