	'en_eve' => 'Placement evening',
	'en_eve_t' => 'First Thursday of each month, 18:30',
	'enquiry_intro' => 'Enquire for a free 45-minute placement interview, or visit the school at Scheepmakerspassage 14, 3011 VH Rotterdam. The form is the way to ask for a place; the phone and email reach the same desk.',
	'alt_s10' => 'Quiet modern street and the entrance of a brick canal-side building',
	'enquiry_h1' => 'Address, hours and how to reach the school',
	'enquiry_b1_1' => 'Kotoba Language is at Scheepmakerspassage 14, 3011 VH Rotterdam, Netherlands. The school was founded in 2016 and teaches English, Dutch, French, German, Mandarin and Japanese at this one address. Write to hello@kotobalanguage.example or call +31 10 555 0142. Opening hours are Monday to Thursday, 09:00–21:00, and Friday, 09:00–17:00.',
	'enquiry_b1_2' => 'On Saturday the school is open 10:00–14:00 for placement interviews only. Sunday is closed. A placement evening is held on the first Thursday of each month at 18:30. The placement interview itself lasts 45 minutes, can be in person or online, and is free. Use the enquiry form to ask for that interview. Say which language you want, and whether you are writing for yourself or for a team.',
	'enquiry_h2' => 'What happens after you enquire',
	'enquiry_b2_1' => 'An enquiry is the first step. Next is the free 45-minute placement interview. You then receive a written level and a track proposal: work, settlement or exam preparation. Enrolment follows, and the registration fee of €45 is paid once. Course fees may be paid in two instalments. Your first class is on one of the four 2026 intakes: 12 January, 13 April, 7 September or 9 November.',
	'enquiry_b2_2' => 'At week 5 of the term the teacher reviews your level with you. Evening courses are €590, the daytime intensive is €880, the exam block is €470, the conversation club is €150, a private lesson is €62, and a workplace group is €1,980. Classes are a maximum of 8. Elias Ferrand advises on placement, and Noor Abadi is director of studies.',
	'en_form_h' => 'Send an enquiry',
	'journal_label' => 'Journal',
	'journal_h1' => 'Journal',
	'journal_intro' => 'The journal collects notes on learning a language in Rotterdam: small classes, placement, and the appointments and meetings the language is for. Each note stays with the way the school actually runs a term.',
	'journal_b1' => 'The journal is a set of short notes from Kotoba Language on learning a language while living and working in Rotterdam. The pieces stay with the school\'s own facts. They describe a class of at most 8, the free 45-minute placement interview, and the level review at week 5. They look at Dutch for appointments, housing and schools, and at English for a team that works across borders. The six languages — English, Dutch, French, German, Mandarin and Japanese — share one building at Scheepmakerspassage 14, 3011 VH Rotterdam, and one list of fees in EUR. The school was founded in 2016. Notes are not a prospectus and they do not rank learners. They record how a term is organised, and what people use the language for once they leave the room.',
	'nf_label' => '404',
	'nf_h1' => 'Page not found',
	'nf_intro' => 'That address does not match a page on this site. You can return home, look through courses and fees, or enquire for a placement interview.',
	'nf_b1' => 'The address you asked for does not match a page at Kotoba Language. The school site carries the courses, the three pathways, the teachers, the fees and the learner stories. Kotoba Language was founded in 2016 and teaches from Scheepmakerspassage 14, 3011 VH Rotterdam, Netherlands. The languages are English, Dutch, French, German, Mandarin and Japanese. Classes have a maximum of 8. If you were looking for a course, the evening course is €590 for 10 weeks, the daytime intensive is €880 for 4 weeks, and a workplace group is €1,980 for a 10-week term on site. The placement interview is free and lasts 45 minutes. You can return to the home page and choose a path from there.',
	'nf_home' => 'Back to the home page',
);
